groups to spare (the module holds all of it) is taken whole;
\code{n_exhausted} counts the module's groups in such strata, where the null
cannot differ from the module.

\strong{Sequential stopping.} Every module gets \code{n_null} draws, then
batches of \code{batch} until \code{h} null draws reach the observed AUROC or
\code{max_draws} are made (Besag & Clifford 1991). Stopping at the \code{h}-th
exceedance makes \code{h / n_draws} the unbiased estimate; the reported
\code{p.val = (1 + n_exceed) / (1 + n_draws)} is the conservative form.
\code{p.val.gt} and \code{p.val.eq} split it into strictly greater and tied
